WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.330
- Free at last.

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:02.700
Free at last!

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.580
Thank God Almighty!

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.381
We are free at last!

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:09.150
(southern blues music)
♪ Crazy, crazy ♪

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.817
♪ Does is crazy ♪

00:00:13.057 --> 00:00:16.974
(suspenseful orchestral music)

00:00:20.423 --> 00:00:23.590
(distant owl hooting)

00:00:25.148 --> 00:00:29.662
(suspenseful music continues)

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.447
(Key gasps)

00:00:32.447 --> 00:00:33.880
- Are you Miss Tubman?

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.343
- The name's Harriet.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.160
- Well, thank God in Heaven

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.360
for the work that you doing, Harriet.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.480
- Before ya thank me,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.573
let me tell ya,

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.780
I've led hundreds of slaves to freedom

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.633
through this here underground railroad,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.803
but it ain't gonna be easy.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.143
Are you ready?

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:57.833
All right.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.960
Then hike up your britches
and follow me to freedom!

00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:10.383
(dramatic orchestral music)
(Harriet yelling and laughing)

00:01:16.331 --> 00:01:19.465
(Key groans)

00:01:19.465 --> 00:01:21.882
(Key grunts)

00:01:24.308 --> 00:01:26.255
Watch this black molasses!

00:01:26.255 --> 00:01:27.088
Ha-ha!

00:01:28.903 --> 00:01:31.948
Yah!

00:01:31.948 --> 00:01:33.258
(Harriet cheers)

00:01:33.258 --> 00:01:36.836
(dramatic music continues)

00:01:36.836 --> 00:01:41.147
- Ow! (groans)

00:01:41.147 --> 00:01:42.639
Well, where is she now?!

00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:46.560
(Harriet yelling)
(glass breaking)

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.430
- That was the easy part.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:49.860
Now, stay close!

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.531
This next 500 miles gets a little sticky.

00:01:53.531 --> 00:01:57.450
(Harriet yipping)
(dramatic music continues)

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.503
- Forget this, man, I'm goin' back.

00:02:01.712 --> 00:02:05.800
(dramatic music continues)

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.060
- Free at last.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.410
Free at last!

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.290
Thank God Almighty!

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.898
We are free at last!

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.898
(audience cheering)

00:02:20.245 --> 00:02:21.078
- [Announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:02:21.078 --> 00:02:22.936
please welcome your next speaker,

00:02:22.936 --> 00:02:24.821
the Reverend Robert Jones.

00:02:24.821 --> 00:02:27.988
(audience applauding)

00:02:32.398 --> 00:02:34.430
- How am I supposed to follow that?

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.760
I can't, nobody can follow that.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.593
How'm I...

00:02:38.961 --> 00:02:39.794
I can't...

00:02:40.872 --> 00:02:42.940
Oh.
(microphone feedback)

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:43.946
All right.

00:02:43.946 --> 00:02:45.180
(microphone feedback)

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.290
Good afternoon, um...

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.640
That, that is the best
speech I've ever heard

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.203
in my entire life!

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.830
Ever!

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.680
I have never heard a
better speech! (laughs)

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.993
And now it is my turn to speak.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.463
Huh. (laughs)

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.090
Who put this running
order together, right?

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.637
You know, um, Dr. King,

00:03:11.637 --> 00:03:14.010
(laughs) he actually covered a lot,

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.410
a lot of what I was gonna say.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:18.920
Um, you know, my, my speech is, uh,

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.220
you're gonna find this funny y'all,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.158
my speech was actually called
"A Vision for the Future."

00:03:24.158 --> 00:03:26.745
(laughs) I'm not saying that
Dr. King copied my speech.

00:03:26.745 --> 00:03:28.270
(audience uproar)
I'm...

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.270
No, no!

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.640
No, I'm saying I'm not saying that!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.417
I'm not saying he tried to copy it!

00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:34.680
Why don't y'all listen

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.360
to what I'm...
(audience uproar)

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.960
Wow! You know what?

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.000
No, come on!
(audience booing)

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.080
I'm just saying! I'm just saying!

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.300
I'm just saying, it's a joke!

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.001
Did I not say it like a joke?

00:03:45.001 --> 00:03:46.403
(audience booing)
Okay!

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.403
Nope?

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.590
Apparently I have six more minutes.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.046
Let's see, red hills of
Georgia, he got that out there.

00:03:56.046 --> 00:03:56.879
Okay...

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.280
Okay, you know what?

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.200
All right, here, here's
somethin', here's somethin' new.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.870
Here's somethin' brand new.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:03.703
How about, okay,

00:04:03.703 --> 00:04:04.760
this is off, me talking off the top

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.640
of my head here, everybody, uh,

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:11.429
how about if we let, uh, black
people enslave white people

00:04:11.429 --> 00:04:12.262
(audience booing)
for okay, you know,

00:04:12.262 --> 00:04:14.854
that sounded a lot better
in my head before I said it.

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.710
(audience booing)
So, that's, uh...

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:17.660
That wouldn't work.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:19.763
Is it warm?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.830
Is anybody else warm?

00:04:23.509 --> 00:04:24.940
Whoo!

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.780
Okay, okay, okay, here's what we gonna do,

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:27.730
here's what we gonna do,

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.360
all right, Dr. King talked about, um, uh,

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.090
all the races coming
together, right, right?

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.790
So, what I want every
negro to do here today

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.430
is find the nearest white
person and give 'em a hug.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:38.928
Just, just give 'em a hug, okay?

00:04:38.928 --> 00:04:39.870
(audience uproar)
Nope, sir.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.720
You're not being attacked,
you're not being attacked,

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.260
you're bein' hugged, okay?

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.830
Everybody take it easy, okay?

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.150
Everybody relax. You know what?

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.950
We don't need 10 negros
hugging one white person, okay?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.960
Let's just, let's, you
know, that's the new rule.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.753
Not ten on one, one on one,

00:04:52.753 --> 00:04:54.507
so we'll just take turns
and everything, okay?

00:04:54.507 --> 00:04:56.190
So, everybody relax, okay?

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.120
Oh my goodness!

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.970
Sir, she doesn't need to be defended!

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.650
She doesn't need to be
defended! She's okay!

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.040
She's okay, okay?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.323
All right, ma'am, okay!

00:05:03.323 --> 00:05:04.714
Officer, is that necessary?!

00:05:04.714 --> 00:05:06.116
I don't think that's necessary, officer!

00:05:06.116 --> 00:05:07.220
No, ma'am! Please!

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.657
Please take it easy, sir!

00:05:08.657 --> 00:05:09.847
Everybody take it easy, all right?!

00:05:09.847 --> 00:05:11.467
These are just hugs,
you're not being attacked!

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:12.303
(water bursting)

00:05:12.303 --> 00:05:13.321
Oh, come on! Stop it!

00:05:13.321 --> 00:05:16.690
What are you doing?! Oh God!
(audience uproar)

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:18.170
- [Announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.870
please turn off your cell
phones and enjoy our production

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.237
of "Lunch with Greatness."

00:05:23.237 --> 00:05:25.330
(paper fluttering)

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.450
- My, my, my!

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.490
What a beautiful day

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.925
in Montgomery, Alabama,
(audience applause)

00:05:29.925 --> 00:05:33.420
I swear the sun is so
hot, I nearly melted.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.750
- Indeed, Dr. King,

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.240
(audience applause)
but I suspect we didn't meet

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:37.790
here to talk about the weather.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.820
- Indeed, Brother Malcolm.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.630
Unless, of course,

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.326
we articulate

00:05:44.326 --> 00:05:48.257
that the sun in this country
shines brighter on some

00:05:48.257 --> 00:05:49.878
than it does on others.

00:05:49.878 --> 00:05:51.545
- [Audience] Mm-hmm.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.890
- Yes, but when the sun does shine on us,

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.911
it is growing the seeds of revolution.

00:06:00.911 --> 00:06:02.034
- Mm-hmm.
- Amen.

00:06:02.034 --> 00:06:04.701
- That's what I'm talkin' about.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.040
- I see your point, Brother Malcolm,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.660
but do not those same
seeds need to be watered

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.841
with love?

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:16.508
- [Audience] Mm-hmm.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.470
- Well, I suppose that is the subject

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.573
of some discussion Dr. King.

00:06:23.426 --> 00:06:25.150
(paper fluttering)
(audience member coughs)

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.140
- And I am all for
discussion Brother Malcolm,

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.720
unless, of course, the words devolve

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.342
into proclamations of hate!

00:06:33.342 --> 00:06:35.850
(audience applauding)

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:40.850
- Well, is that not why we
are here today, Dr. King?

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:43.053
To discuss.

00:06:44.188 --> 00:06:49.188
(fly buzzing)
(paper fluttering)

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.100
- Yes, Brother Malcolm.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.951
And I am confident that as we discuss-

00:06:54.951 --> 00:06:57.313
- Oh, we are going to discuss it

00:06:57.313 --> 00:06:59.180
and discuss it

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.580
until

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.360
I say

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.193
that

00:07:04.359 --> 00:07:07.830
our people have never resorted to violence

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.870
before the white man gave them no choice

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:15.038
but to pay him back in the
only currency he understands!

00:07:15.038 --> 00:07:18.038
(audience cheering)

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.393
- Brother Malcolm,

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:26.550
is that what you really
have to say at this point

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.860
in our lunch?

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.090
- Indeed, Dr. King,

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.470
because we didn't land on Plymouth Rock,

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.198
Plymouth Rock landed on us!

00:07:36.198 --> 00:07:39.198
(audience cheering)

00:07:40.175 --> 00:07:42.940
- That's the truth!
- Amen!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.930
- Okay, well, yes, all right, yeah,

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.040
I've heard you say that before.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.570
I don't know why we're
talking about rocks,

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:55.450
when in fact, it is the flesh
and the bone and the dreams...

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:59.470
I have a dream that someday
our children will be judged

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.100
by the content of their character,

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.699
not by the color of their skin!

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:05.653
(audience cheering)

00:08:05.653 --> 00:08:07.750
- Yep, yep, yep, yep, same for me!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:08.583
Same for me!

00:08:08.583 --> 00:08:09.416
In fact,

00:08:09.416 --> 00:08:11.590
I believe that one day a black man

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.325
will become the president of
the United States of America!

00:08:14.325 --> 00:08:16.110
(audience cheering)

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.546
Hopefully for eight years!

00:08:17.546 --> 00:08:19.303
(audience cheers)

00:08:19.303 --> 00:08:20.136
Obama, 2012.

00:08:20.136 --> 00:08:23.136
(audience applauds)

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.660
- Oh, of course eight years,
of course eight years!

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:27.639
That's a given, right?

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:29.690
(laughs) That's a given, you know?

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.750
I mean, but in order to get there,

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:33.900
isn't he going to need the help

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:37.210
of our strong, beautiful black women?!

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:38.932
(audience cheering)

00:08:38.932 --> 00:08:43.350
Gotta respect the sisters!
Gotta respect the sisters!

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:44.750
Gotta respect the sisters.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.925
(audience applause)

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:49.337
- As Wesley Snipes said in "Passenger 57,"

00:08:49.337 --> 00:08:51.228
"Always bet on black!"

00:08:51.228 --> 00:08:54.261
Yeah!
(audience cheering)

00:08:54.261 --> 00:08:56.770
(all cheering)

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:57.770
- West side!

00:08:58.619 --> 00:08:59.452
West side!

00:09:00.391 --> 00:09:03.474
(cheering continues)

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:08.033
- And that's what we're here to say,

00:09:08.033 --> 00:09:11.240
is that we are the new
Black Panther Party.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.430
- [Interviewer] What's the biggest problem

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.110
facing the movement?

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:14.943
- Well, you know,

00:09:14.943 --> 00:09:16.440
we supposed to be in this era

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.930
of so-called post-racial harmony
with all people in America,

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:24.000
but us blacks are being
murdered all over the place

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.630
and we get the same treatment
time and time again!

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.610
We're not even second class citizens.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.130
We third class!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.290
Stand up, Black America,

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:34.970
and declare to white America

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.320
that we aren't gonna take this no more.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:38.153
Okay?

00:09:38.153 --> 00:09:39.750
- [Interviewer] Why come
out now and say this?

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.583
- You know what?

00:09:40.583 --> 00:09:44.550
You had 400 years to
get it right, America,

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.590
but you don't know how
to treat your people,

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:47.790
all people!

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.370
It's time to stand up!

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.960
It's time to take back!

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.420
It's time for us to fight back!

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.440
And we won't take your
phony words anymore,

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.390
we're not gonna do it.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:59.240
We want concrete results!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.250
No, you, you, you hear
what we're saying to you?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.660
United snakes of America!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.870
What are you supposed to do

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.490
when the whole world is watching

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:08.920
and no one is saying anything?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.500
We will not be silent!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.570
- [Interviewer] Okay, you sir,

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:14.003
anything you wanted to say?

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:16.830
- Oh, me? No, I'm good.

00:10:18.821 --> 00:10:21.821
(upbeat beatboxing)

00:10:24.205 --> 00:10:26.647
♪ All I want, yeah ♪

00:10:26.647 --> 00:10:28.612
♪ But I don't need you ♪

